45,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":false,"_score_margin_vs_hist":0.0,"_gate_piotroski":5,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":-0.09270892980754633,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":6.7973819342542745,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":0.22979272102352655,"_gp_incr_roic":true,"_score_incr_roic":93.3,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.1532749950082293,"_gp_margin_advantage":true,"_score_margin_advantage":84.4,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":0.3377890076035357,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":100.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":-0.06102055159846824,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0.0028895693270318845,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":2.9,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.006957250833979693,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":18.8,"_gate_share_shrink":0.006505579410817086,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":41.9,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.008667512958595905,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":85.6,"_gate_insider_own":0.0114400005,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":7.6,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"FTAI Aviation Ltd. owns, acquires, and sells aviation equipment for the transportation of goods and people worldwide. It operates in two segments, Aviation Leasing and Aerospace Products. The Aviation Leasing segment owns, leases, manages, and sells aircraft and aircraft engines. As of December 31, 2025, this segment owned and managed 290 aviation assets consisting of 47 commercial aircraft and 243 engines, including eight aircraft and seventeen engines in Russia. The Aerospace Products segment develops, manufactures, repairs/refurbishes, and sells aircraft engines and aftermarket components for the commercial aircraft engines. It also engages in the offshore energy business, which consists of vessels and equipment that support offshore oil and gas activities and production. FTAI Aviation Ltd. has a strategic collaboration with Aeronautical Engineers, Inc. The company was founded in 2011 and is headquartered in New York, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Joseph P. Adams Jr. | Chairman & CEO | Age 67 | Compensation: $3.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 985 people. Revenue per employee of $2.5M ranks in the top quartile among Industrials peers, with revenue growing 34%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $22K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["FTAI Aviation Ltd. is a large-cap industrials business with a $18.4B market cap on $2.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +52% over the past three years and +34% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 0% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $338M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Accruals are elevated at +18.0% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 2.4\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.7%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 2.2\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Accruals elevated at +18.0% of assets \u2014 Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (15.1% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Carries a 65% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.6489425981873111},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 15% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","10 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Growing faster than most Industrials peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Capital International Investors Reveals 13.0% Ownership Stake in FTAI Aviation","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/capital-international-investors-reveals-130-ownership-stake-in-ftai-aviation","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794586819.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{"title":"FTAI Aviation Ltd. $FTAI Shares Bought by Ethic Inc.","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/ftai-aviation-ltd-ftai-shares-bought-by-ethic-inc.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794476779.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.878,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Price-Driven Insight from (FTAI) for Rule-Based Strategy","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/15/Price-Driven_Insight_from_FTAI_for_Rule-Based_Strategy_111126100002_1794409202.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794409202.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"FTAI Aviation Stock In Focus After Earnings And Dividend Declaration","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/capital-goods/nasdaq-ftai/ftai-aviation/news/ftai-aviation-stock-in-focus-after-earnings-and-dividend-dec","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794389027.465,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.296,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","dividend"]},{"title":"Financial Survey: FTAI Aviation (NASDAQ:FTAI) vs. Huntington Ingalls Industries (NYSE:HII)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/08/financial-survey-ftai-aviation-nasdaqftai-vs-huntington-ingalls-industries-nysehii.html","date":"2026-11-08","timestamp":1794131343.0,"origin":"tiin